# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in your own values. Never commit
# a real debug token — each is a per-developer secret registered in the
# Firebase console (App Check > your web app > Manage debug tokens).

# O-3 App Check (docs/O3_APP_CHECK_RULING_2026-07-13.md): local dev needs a
# debug token since localhost isn't an allowed domain on the App Check
# reCAPTCHA Enterprise key. Leave unset to auto-generate one on first run —
# the SDK prints it to the browser console; register that value in the
# console instead.
VITE_APPCHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN=

# Sentry crash reporting for the Kinfolk portal at kinfolk.tribetails.com.
# OPTIONAL: leave empty and reporting stays disabled (the app logs
# "Sentry disabled: no VITE_SENTRY_DSN" and runs normally). To activate, paste
# the client DSN from the Sentry project (Settings > Client Keys / DSN) at
# https://auntieos-ttpc.sentry.io.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is REQUIRED, and it is also why this cannot live in Secret
# Manager. Vite INLINES import.meta.env.VITE_* into the JavaScript bundle at
# BUILD time; there is no server process to inject a secret into at runtime, so
# the value must be present when `vite build` runs, and it then ships inside the
# bundle every browser downloads. That is fine: a Sentry DSN is a public client
# key by design, permitting write-only event ingestion. Abuse is handled by
# Sentry-side rate limits and inbound filters, not by secrecy.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Mapbox public token for the KinCare route map (#520). It draws the visit
# route over real streets instead of a bare line on an empty background.
# OPTIONAL: leave empty and RouteMap keeps drawing the SVG polyline it always
# has. No error, no blank frame, just the plainer map.
#
# Use the URL-restricted `web-maps-public` token (scopes styles:tiles,
# styles:read, fonts:read; referrers kinfolk.tribetails.com and
# auntie.tribetails.com), NOT the unrestricted mobile one the Android apps use.
#
# Same VITE_ mechanics as the DSN above: Vite inlines it at BUILD time, so it
# ships in the bundle every browser downloads and cannot live in Secret
# Manager. A `pk.*` token is a public client credential by design; it is
# read-only, and what bounds the value of an extracted copy is the referrer
# restriction plus rotation, not secrecy.
VITE_MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN=
